 ### Procedural SDF Primitives
-Perlin or Simplex noise can be treated as an SDF because it returns a real number at every point in space and is locally smooth [S12, unofficial]. To create a height map terrain, ignore the z value in the noise function and define the surface as all points where z equals the noise value at (x, y, 0) [S12, unofficial]. To add overhangs or caves, implement 3D noise functions using all values. Subtract from the surface for caves or add to empty space for terrain with overhangs [S12, unofficial]. When iterating over all 3 dimensions for 3D noise, add fall-off values to reduce the area to compute because it is more expensive [S12, unofficial]. Formula: `surface_perlin = all x, y, z such that Perlin(x, y, z) = 0` [S12, unofficial].
